Subject: register VM slims the JS-to-JS call frame record

What this does:
  A record frame (`JSRegRun`) carried several fields that nothing in the register
  VM ever reads: `rt` (the only `->rt` access in the VM), the transfer form's
  `set_d`/`set_s` (the `regvm_t_move_xfer_slow` handler that read them no longer
  exists) and `func_obj` (a duplicate of `sf->cur_func`, whose one reader, the
  `super` path of `init_ctor`, now goes through the frame). `rec->ctx` is read
  only by the register-file consistency checker, so its store is compiled only
  under `QJS_REGVM_RCCHECK`. `sf->cur_sp` is never read for a record frame either
  (only async state's frame and the stack VM use it), so the record fill no
  longer clears it.

  `regvm_record_fill`, the entry-record setup and the in-loop rebind all drop the
  corresponding stores; the struct shrinks by four members.

  Measured (`fixed.js`, i7-8700), interleaved against 0151:
  22,760.2/22,760.6 M -> 22,577.0/22,579.3 M instructions (**-0.182 G, -0.80 %**),
  cycles 10,897/10,954 M -> 10,850/10,863 M. Full gate 8 pass / 0 fail:
  22,577,121,551 / 10,827,075,131; box2d checksum exact; diff-suite 398/0/0 mono
  and threaded; leak assertion clean; peak RSS 13244 KB; test262 errors 50 (<= 64).
